      "title": "Controls",
      "id": 4,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 11
      },
      "description": "The relay's controls need the admin token in a request header, which Grafana keeps in the datasource, out of the browser's reach. They live on the dashboard.",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "## Controls are on the dashboard\n\n### [Open the dashboard &rarr;](/)\n\nSend a lobby to a page, restart a match, take the CSV: all of it is there, on the same hostname.\n\n---\n\n**Why not here.** Every control endpoint is a POST that needs the admin token in a header. Grafana keeps that token inside the datasource, where only its backend can read it -- which is what keeps an operator credential out of the browser. A button drawn on this page runs in the browser and has no way to reach it.\n\nThis page is for watching: the log on the left, who is where on the right, both refreshed every second."
      }
